1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,457
The computer monitor in my darkened
bedroom flickered, bleeding

2
00:00:05,477 --> 00:00:11,147
from a game of Solitaire into a field of
pure, obsidian black.

3
00:00:11,167 --> 00:00:15,858
Then the crimson letters began to carve
themselves across

4
00:00:15,878 --> 00:00:19,945
the glass: Hi Jack, I need a favor from
you.

5
00:00:19,965 --> 00:00:25,061
The internet cable was completely
disconnected, its severed

6
00:00:25,081 --> 00:00:30,264
connector lying limp on the carpet, yet
the machine answered

7
00:00:30,284 --> 00:00:34,986
my thoughts as if it were breathing inside
my head.

8
00:00:35,006 --> 00:00:40,170
It promised me wealth, love, and
effortless promotions

9
00:00:40,190 --> 00:00:44,460
in exchange for tiny, harmless gestures.

10
00:00:44,480 --> 00:00:51,158
Twelve years later, sitting in my
sprawling country home with the woman of

11
00:00:51,178 --> 00:00:57,885
my dreams asleep downstairs, the monitor
lit up with one final message.

12
00:00:57,905 --> 00:01:04,510
It told me that every person I ever doomed
had been a brushstroke in an unseen

13
00:01:04,530 --> 00:01:10,905
masterpiece, and that tonight, the canvas
would be completed in blood.

14
00:01:10,925 --> 00:01:15,912
Would you give up eighty-five bitter years
for twelve perfect ones?

15
00:01:15,932 --> 00:01:17,704
Let us go back to the beginning.

16
00:01:18,304 --> 00:01:24,003
The strange communication began on a damp
Tuesday evening while

17
00:01:24,023 --> 00:01:29,387
I was sitting alone in my modest
second-floor apartment.

18
00:01:29,407 --> 00:01:34,312
Rain tapped incessantly against the window
panes, and the

19
00:01:34,332 --> 00:01:39,410
blinking amber light on my router signaled
that my internet

20
00:01:39,430 --> 00:01:44,094
connection was down for the third time
that week.

21
00:01:44,114 --> 00:01:49,230
As I dragged the virtual cards across the
screen, the Solitaire

22
00:01:49,250 --> 00:01:53,280
game suddenly dissolved into pitch-black
void.

23
00:01:53,300 --> 00:02:01,669
Bright red monospaced text appeared line
by line: Hi Jack, I need a favor from you.

24
00:02:01,689 --> 00:02:06,283
You are a very special person, and I know
you will help me.

25
00:02:06,303 --> 00:02:12,819
A cold shiver crept down my spine as I
leaned forward in my desk chair.

26
00:02:12,839 --> 00:02:18,800
I thought it was a prank, but when I
reached behind the tower and pulled

27
00:02:18,820 --> 00:02:24,981
the ethernet cable entirely from the wall,
the screen did not falter.

28
00:02:25,001 --> 00:02:30,034
Still here, Jack, the text printed in
eerie, steady rhythm.

29
00:02:30,054 --> 00:02:35,113
Tomorrow when you arrive at work, I need
you to move the large

30
00:02:35,133 --> 00:02:39,836
potted plant next to the elevator on the
ground floor.

31
00:02:39,856 --> 00:02:46,485
Pull it out exactly three inches from the
wall at eight seventeen in the morning.

32
00:02:46,505 --> 00:02:51,832
The text promised that no one would be in
the lobby at that precise

33
00:02:51,852 --> 00:02:57,160
second, and that I would be richly
rewarded for my cooperation.

34
00:02:57,180 --> 00:03:01,247
Panicked, I yanked the main power cord
from the wall

35
00:03:01,267 --> 00:03:05,548
socket, plunging the room into absolute
darkness.

36
00:03:05,568 --> 00:03:10,367
I lay awake in bed for hours, convincing
myself that

37
00:03:10,387 --> 00:03:15,022
exhaustion was playing cruel tricks on my
mind.

38
00:03:15,042 --> 00:03:19,749
Yet by morning, fear had subtly
transformed into

39
00:03:19,769 --> 00:03:23,709
an overwhelming, irresistible curiosity.

40
00:03:24,309 --> 00:03:29,099
I arrived at the corporate office park at
ten minutes past

41
00:03:29,119 --> 00:03:33,628
eight, parking my sedan at the far edge of
the lot.

42
00:03:33,648 --> 00:03:39,028
At precisely eight sixteen, I walked
through the revolving glass

43
00:03:39,048 --> 00:03:44,541
doors into the soaring marble atrium of
the ten-story tower.

44
00:03:44,561 --> 00:03:50,208
To my astonishment, the normally bustling
lobby was completely

45
00:03:50,228 --> 00:03:55,535
desolate, exactly as the midnight message
had foretold.

46
00:03:55,555 --> 00:04:00,794
Heart pounding against my ribs, I
approached the towering ceramic

47
00:04:00,814 --> 00:04:05,451
pot nestled between the two central
elevator shafts.

48
00:04:05,471 --> 00:04:09,997
The ornamental ficus plant was
surprisingly heavy,

49
00:04:10,017 --> 00:04:14,388
filled with dense river rocks and moist
soil.

50
00:04:14,408 --> 00:04:20,037
Bracing my heels against the polished
marble, I hauled the pot forward

51
00:04:20,057 --> 00:04:24,926
exactly three inches and stepped back into
the shadows.

52
00:04:24,946 --> 00:04:31,797
Seconds later, the outer glass doors
opened and the morning wave of commuters

53
00:04:31,817 --> 00:04:38,343
poured inside, walking past the shifted
plant without a second glance.

54
00:04:38,363 --> 00:04:45,383
I rode the elevator up to the seventh
floor, settled into my cubicle, and waited

55
00:04:45,403 --> 00:04:52,697
for some supernatural consequence, but the
morning remained mundane and quiet.

56
00:04:52,717 --> 00:04:59,147
My only genuine joy at the company was
Allie, a radiant, warm-hearted

57
00:04:59,167 --> 00:05:04,776
woman who occupied the workstation just
across the aisle.

58
00:05:04,796 --> 00:05:09,749
For months, our brief morning
conversations had been the

59
00:05:09,769 --> 00:05:14,298
solitary anchor keeping my lonely
existence afloat.

60
00:05:14,898 --> 00:05:18,727
As Allie and I were laughing over morning
coffee,

61
00:05:18,746 --> 00:05:22,875
the elevator doors chime echoed down the
hallway.

62
00:05:22,895 --> 00:05:28,771
Out hobbled James Bentley, the stern and
demanding manager of our

63
00:05:28,791 --> 00:05:34,573
entire division, leaning heavily against
the beige drywall.

64
00:05:34,593 --> 00:05:40,507
Bentley was swearing loudly in agony, his
face pale and contorted

65
00:05:40,527 --> 00:05:45,828
as he dragged his swollen right foot
across the carpet.

66
00:05:45,848 --> 00:05:50,235
When Allie rushed over with concern, he
barked that he

67
00:05:50,255 --> 00:05:54,398
had tripped over a carelessly positioned
decorative

68
00:05:54,418 --> 00:05:59,010
plant in the lobby and violently twisted
his ankle.

69
00:05:59,030 --> 00:06:05,087
A wave of sickening guilt washed over me
as I retreated to my desk.

70
00:06:05,107 --> 00:06:11,381
Moving that pot three inches had caused my
manager to stumble, an innocent

71
00:06:11,401 --> 00:06:17,615
mistake that I desperately hoped would
heal with a few days of rest.

72
00:06:17,635 --> 00:06:21,783
When I returned home that evening, the
computer screen

73
00:06:21,803 --> 00:06:25,788
flickered to life the moment I entered the
room.

74
00:06:25,808 --> 00:06:27,650
How was your day, Jack?

75
00:06:27,670 --> 00:06:31,500
the red letters asked with mocking
politeness.

76
00:06:31,520 --> 00:06:36,583
I sat motionless as the text continued:
You are wondering

77
00:06:36,603 --> 00:06:40,539
why James Bentley had to twist his ankle.

78
00:06:40,559 --> 00:06:44,349
This chain of events is not done playing
out.

79
00:06:44,369 --> 00:06:48,218
Go to work tomorrow as you always do, and
watch

80
00:06:48,238 --> 00:06:51,960
how smoothly the pieces fall into place.

81
00:06:51,980 --> 00:06:58,555
A disturbing mixture of terror and dark
fascination took hold of me, and

82
00:06:58,575 --> 00:07:04,528
that night, my sleep was haunted by the
sound of falling dominos.

83
00:07:05,128 --> 00:07:10,023
The following afternoon at the office was
unusually somber.

84
00:07:10,043 --> 00:07:15,450
James Bentley arrived after lunch, his
ankle heavily bandaged,

85
00:07:15,470 --> 00:07:20,452
barely able to bear any weight on the
swollen joint.

86
00:07:20,472 --> 00:07:24,092
Shortly before three o'clock, Bentley
limped

87
00:07:24,112 --> 00:07:28,032
over to Allie's cubicle in obvious
distress.

88
00:07:28,052 --> 00:07:34,801
He pleaded with her to drive his car to an
urgent care clinic, explaining that

89
00:07:34,821 --> 00:07:41,760
the throbbing pain had made it impossible
for him to operate the gas pedal.

90
00:07:41,780 --> 00:07:47,601
Allie agreed without hesitation, grabbing
her winter coat from the chair.

91
00:07:47,621 --> 00:07:53,734
She turned back to flash me a gentle
smile, whispering, See you tomorrow,

92
00:07:53,754 --> 00:07:59,393
Jackie, as she escorted our limping boss
toward the elevators.

93
00:07:59,413 --> 00:08:03,424
Ten minutes later, a catastrophic sound
shattered

94
00:08:03,444 --> 00:08:07,591
the afternoon tranquility of the seventh
floor.

95
00:08:07,611 --> 00:08:12,656
A deafening air horn blared in frantic
bursts, followed by

96
00:08:12,676 --> 00:08:17,634
the agonizing screech of burning rubber
and a thunderous,

97
00:08:17,654 --> 00:08:22,713
violent metallic impact that shook the
glass windows.

98
00:08:22,733 --> 00:08:26,676
Workers gasped and surged toward the
panoramic

99
00:08:26,696 --> 00:08:30,250
glass overlooking the boulevard below.

100
00:08:30,270 --> 00:08:36,462
Down on the asphalt, an eighteen-wheeler
truck had plowed broadside into

101
00:08:36,482 --> 00:08:42,520
Bentley's sedan, crushing the driver's
side like an aluminum can.

102
00:08:42,540 --> 00:08:48,032
I scrambled down the emergency stairs in
blind panic, bursting

103
00:08:48,052 --> 00:08:53,755
onto the street amidst wailing sirens and
weeping bystanders.

104
00:08:53,775 --> 00:08:58,958
James Bentley sat dazed and bleeding in
the passenger seat,

105
00:08:58,978 --> 00:09:04,338
but the driver's compartment where Allie
had been sitting had

106
00:09:04,358 --> 00:09:09,727
been compacted into twisted,
unrecognizable scrap metal.

107
00:09:09,747 --> 00:09:12,429
I did not return to the office that day.

108
00:09:12,449 --> 00:09:17,325
I drove back to my apartment in a numb
daze, vomiting

109
00:09:17,345 --> 00:09:22,314
into the sink as the unbearable truth
crushed my soul:

110
00:09:22,334 --> 00:09:26,953
my hands had set that fatal collision into
motion.

111
00:09:27,553 --> 00:09:31,715
I stared at the computer for nearly an
hour before

112
00:09:31,735 --> 00:09:35,611
trembling fingers pressed the power
switch.

113
00:09:35,631 --> 00:09:40,197
The display ignited instantly into that
horrific

114
00:09:40,217 --> 00:09:44,606
black field: No Jack, it is not your
fault.

115
00:09:44,626 --> 00:09:49,772
All people die eventually, some simply
sooner than others.

116
00:09:49,792 --> 00:09:55,083
The text explained that Allie had been
secretly unfaithful to

117
00:09:55,103 --> 00:10:01,003
her past partners and was planning to
manipulate my naive affections

118
00:10:01,023 --> 00:10:05,743
into four agonizing years of emotional
devastation.

119
00:10:05,763 --> 00:10:09,792
It insisted that by shifting the timeline,
we had

120
00:10:09,812 --> 00:10:13,712
spared me a lifetime of bitter heartbreak.

121
00:10:13,732 --> 00:10:21,259
Enraged by the cold rationalization, I
seized the CRT monitor and hurled it onto

122
00:10:21,279 --> 00:10:28,352
the hardwood floor, watching it shatter
into sparks and smoking plastic.

123
00:10:28,372 --> 00:10:33,687
Yet the next morning, reality took an even
more disorienting turn.

124
00:10:33,707 --> 00:10:41,204
Division Director Diego Salbara called me
into the executive boardroom and offered

125
00:10:41,224 --> 00:10:48,262
me James Bentley's managerial role on the
spot, citing the critical Lancaster

126
00:10:48,282 --> 00:10:55,404
project that could not pause while Bentley
lay in an intensive care coma.

127
00:10:55,424 --> 00:11:02,625
The promotion doubled my salary overnight
and vaulted me into executive leadership.

128
00:11:02,645 --> 00:11:06,900
That afternoon, I purchased a brand new
flat-panel

129
00:11:06,920 --> 00:11:10,513
display and hooked it up in my study.

130
00:11:10,533 --> 00:11:16,240
The red text welcomed me back with warmth:
I am called the Seer.

131
00:11:16,260 --> 00:11:20,367
For thousands of years I have seen all
branching

132
00:11:20,387 --> 00:11:23,935
futures, what will be and what can be.

133
00:11:23,955 --> 00:11:28,951
But without a physical body, I require a
living partner to

134
00:11:28,971 --> 00:11:34,071
act as my paintbrush upon the canvas of
human history.

135
00:11:34,091 --> 00:11:40,251
The entity swore two unbreakable oaths: it
would never speak an outright

136
00:11:40,271 --> 00:11:45,701
lie, and it would never command me to
commit an illegal act.

137
00:11:45,721 --> 00:11:51,383
Transfixed by the promise of unlimited
fortune, I placed my hands

138
00:11:51,403 --> 00:11:56,123
on the keys and typed: What do you want me
to do next?

139
00:11:56,723 --> 00:12:02,558
Two years passed in a whirlwind of
ascending prosperity, with small

140
00:12:02,578 --> 00:12:07,752
monthly requests arriving like clockwork
on my terminal.

141
00:12:07,772 --> 00:12:12,777
One afternoon, the Seer instructed me to
enter Garmin's

142
00:12:12,797 --> 00:12:17,711
Liquor Store downtown at precisely twelve
thirty-seven

143
00:12:17,731 --> 00:12:23,004
and answer any question with the number
twenty-seven.

144
00:12:23,024 --> 00:12:28,727
Inside the dingy shop, a burly
construction worker in dusty overalls

145
00:12:28,747 --> 00:12:33,572
was filling out a state lottery ticket at
the counter.

146
00:12:33,592 --> 00:12:38,371
When the man turned around and casually
asked me for

147
00:12:38,391 --> 00:12:43,528
a lucky number, I smiled and replied:
Twenty-seven.

148
00:12:43,548 --> 00:12:48,760
Two weeks later, the same worker spotted
me in a supermarket,

149
00:12:48,780 --> 00:12:54,035
beaming with joy and wearing an expensive
gold wristwatch.

150
00:12:54,055 --> 00:12:59,822
He shouted that he had won the
multi-million dollar jackpot, writing

151
00:12:59,842 --> 00:13:06,061
me a personal check for ten thousand
dollars as his good luck charm.

152
00:13:06,081 --> 00:13:12,768
When I asked the Seer why we had finally
performed an act of pure benevolence,

153
00:13:12,788 --> 00:13:18,614
the screen illuminated with cold clarity:
Within twenty-four months,

154
00:13:18,634 --> 00:13:24,589
that lottery winner will squander every
penny on reckless gambles.

155
00:13:24,609 --> 00:13:31,532
His wife will flee with their children,
leaving him an impoverished, broken shell.

156
00:13:31,552 --> 00:13:37,982
Another favor instructed me to park my car
in stall forty-three outside

157
00:13:38,002 --> 00:13:43,641
the County Courthouse at four forty-seven
in the afternoon.

158
00:13:43,661 --> 00:13:49,541
That simple act displaced another driver,
initiating a sprawling

159
00:13:49,561 --> 00:13:54,797
chain reaction across twenty-five
strangers that resulted

160
00:13:54,817 --> 00:14:00,225
in a missed train, a mugging, and an
emergency detour.

161
00:14:00,245 --> 00:14:06,737
At the end of that tangled web stood
Donna, a brilliant, compassionate woman

162
00:14:06,757 --> 00:14:13,120
who entered the courthouse lobby at the
exact second I was walking out.

163
00:14:13,140 --> 00:14:17,319
We fell deeply in love, married within the
year, and

164
00:14:17,339 --> 00:14:21,565
built a life filled with laughter and
devotion.

165
00:14:21,585 --> 00:14:28,263
Over twelve glorious years, every request
bore the same twin fruits: an

166
00:14:28,283 --> 00:14:34,603
unseen disaster for a stranger, and
radiant, golden fortune for me.

167
00:14:35,203 --> 00:14:41,184
By our twelfth year together, Donna and I
were living in a magnificent

168
00:14:41,204 --> 00:14:47,057
two-story estate nestled among the pine
trees of the countryside.

169
00:14:47,077 --> 00:14:52,048
I had retired early, surrounded by wealth,
deep respect,

170
00:14:52,068 --> 00:14:56,597
and a marriage that felt like heaven on
earth.

171
00:14:56,617 --> 00:15:01,713
On a chilly November evening, while Donna
was relaxing on the

172
00:15:01,733 --> 00:15:06,962
living room sofa, my computer chimed in
the upstairs study.

173
00:15:06,982 --> 00:15:13,845
The Seer's request was simpler than ever:
Call Riago's Pizza in exactly

174
00:15:13,865 --> 00:15:19,723
two minutes, let the line ring three
times, and hang up.

175
00:15:19,743 --> 00:15:24,263
I dialed the number, counted three hollow
rings over the

176
00:15:24,283 --> 00:15:28,859
speaker, and ended the call without a
second thought.

177
00:15:28,879 --> 00:15:34,513
Thirty minutes later, the front doorbell
chimed through the quiet halls.

178
00:15:34,533 --> 00:15:39,998
Standing on the front porch was a pizza
delivery courier whose

179
00:15:40,018 --> 00:15:45,784
sheer physical presence sent a pang of
dread through my chest.

180
00:15:45,804 --> 00:15:53,317
He was a towering young man, well over six
feet six inches tall, with broad,

181
00:15:53,337 --> 00:16:00,903
muscular shoulders and hollow, furious
eyes under a stained Riago's cap.

182
00:16:00,923 --> 00:16:05,954
The courier shoved a cardboard pizza box
into my hands,

183
00:16:05,974 --> 00:16:11,097
snarling that it was already paid by card
and he refused

184
00:16:11,117 --> 00:16:15,530
to drive it back down the dark rural
highway.

185
00:16:15,550 --> 00:16:22,445
When I admitted that I carried no cash on
me for a tip, the boy spat venomously into

186
00:16:22,465 --> 00:16:29,399
the flowerbed, glared into the hallway,
and stormed back to his idling vehicle.

187
00:16:29,419 --> 00:16:33,942
Donna and I ate the pizza together on the
plush couch,

188
00:16:33,962 --> 00:16:38,785
laughing as the rain drummed softly
against the glass.

189
00:16:38,805 --> 00:16:42,954
Shortly after eleven, she drifted to sleep
under

190
00:16:42,974 --> 00:16:47,573
a knitted blanket, looking peaceful and
radiant.

191
00:16:47,593 --> 00:16:53,399
Leaving Donna sleeping soundly, I tiptoed
upstairs to my office,

192
00:16:53,419 --> 00:16:58,244
an inexplicable knot of anxiety tightening
in my gut.

193
00:16:58,844 --> 00:17:05,410
As soon as I sat down, the monitor flashed
into that familiar crimson glow:

194
00:17:05,430 --> 00:17:11,418
That delivery boy is quite an impressive
specimen, isn't he Jack?

195
00:17:11,438 --> 00:17:16,638
He noticed that you forgot to lock the
heavy front door after he left.

196
00:17:16,658 --> 00:17:22,797
Panic seized my limbs, but the text
commanded: Stay seated, Jack.

197
00:17:22,817 --> 00:17:27,870
Locking the door now will not alter the
geometry of fate.

198
00:17:27,890 --> 00:17:33,701
You see, every single favor you carried
out across twelve years

199
00:17:33,721 --> 00:17:39,056
was directed toward one supreme artistic
culmination.

200
00:17:39,076 --> 00:17:45,108
The Seer unraveled the horrifying
tapestry: when Allie died twelve years

201
00:17:45,128 --> 00:17:51,328
ago, her devastated brother dropped out of
medical school and never became

202
00:17:51,348 --> 00:17:56,923
the child psychologist who could have
healed that troubled boy.

203
00:17:56,943 --> 00:18:02,330
The ruined lottery winner had moved into
the boy's neighborhood,

204
00:18:02,350 --> 00:18:06,582
beating him mercilessly in an alcoholic
rage.

205
00:18:06,602 --> 00:18:13,385
The boy's neglectful mother had fallen
into severe addiction using narcotics

206
00:18:13,405 --> 00:18:19,951
purchased by the very mugger displaced by
my courthouse parking favor.

207
00:18:19,971 --> 00:18:25,645
Over a decade of calculated suffering had
engineered that young

208
00:18:25,665 --> 00:18:30,886
man into an unstoppable instrument of
psychotic fury.

209
00:18:30,906 --> 00:18:37,648
Tonight, a wrong address and a missing tip
pushed his fragile mind over the edge.

210
00:18:37,668 --> 00:18:42,366
The text concluded: He is standing in your
living room

211
00:18:42,386 --> 00:18:47,359
right now, ending Donna's life at this
exact second.

212
00:18:47,379 --> 00:18:51,615
A muffled, choked scream echoed up the
stairwell,

213
00:18:51,635 --> 00:18:55,998
followed by the sickening wet sound of
silence.

214
00:18:56,018 --> 00:19:02,388
I shrieked Donna's name and lunged toward
the doorway, but a melodic,

215
00:19:02,408 --> 00:19:08,302
feminine voice suddenly resonated directly
inside my skull.

216
00:19:08,322 --> 00:19:12,776
Stop, Jack, the soothing whisper echoed in
my mind.

217
00:19:12,796 --> 00:19:14,345
You cannot save her.

218
00:19:14,365 --> 00:19:19,448
Had we never met, you would have lived
eighty-five bitter,

219
00:19:19,468 --> 00:19:24,587
lonely, meaningless years, dying unloved
and forgotten.

220
